    "safety_allocation": "NOT_PROVIDED: no owner safety scope recorded for the TIM benchmark work orders"
  },
  "scope": [
    "HAL (classic, handle-based) as delivered by ST: TIM_HandleTypeDef with its Instance (the CMSIS device structure TIM2, stm32n6xx.h) and Init configuration (TIM_Base_InitTypeDef); HAL_StatusTypeDef results; the HAL framework headers and ST's stm32n6xx_hal_conf_template.h configured with the TIM module and the DMA module headers the handle type needs (USE_FULL_ASSERT off, as delivered)",
    "Time-base initialisation and de-initialisation from the handle configuration (prescaler TIM_PSC, counter mode TIM_CR1.DIR/CMS, period TIM_ARR, clock division TIM_CR1.CKD, auto-reload preload TIM_CR1.ARPE; the update generation that loads them, TIM_EGR.UG); start and stop of the counter in polling mode (TIM_CR1.CEN); a software event generation (TIM_EGR); the handle state",
    "Out of scope: the MSP hooks (weak, empty as delivered), interrupt and DMA modes, output compare/PWM/input capture/one-pulse/encoder channels, clock source and slave configuration, the extended API, register callbacks"
  ],
